{"author":{"id":"6af04b5756f10b3005a23338b8f25a6c1d7564fe1ddddc77e70806b2f14ac31a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789499605,"nonce":"fixjH7noVdL1T1h6vJ74GkzgtPY=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOUKdEis8AAAABRdHiBg","github-url":"https://github.com/ff6347/gic-lang/issues/37","origin":"github"},"title":"Spike the Electron application and Pi boundary","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nBuild disposable evidence for hosting the shared GIC web application in a packaged Electron window and for running the minimal Pi agent/provider libraries outside the renderer. Compare the result with the Tauri spike without assuming Electron should be selected. The renderer must remain sandboxed and receive only operation-specific document and tutor messages through a narrow preload API.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A packaged macOS application launches built assets without a development server or separately managed process.\n- [ ] The renderer has `nodeIntegration: false`, `contextIsolation: true`, and sandboxing enabled.\n- [ ] A context-isolated preload exposes only explicit Open, Save, Save As, tutor probe, and lifecycle operations.\n- [ ] Native Open, Save, and Save As round-trip one `.gic` document without exposing arbitrary Node, filesystem, shell, IPC, or credential APIs to the renderer.\n- [ ] `@mariozechner/pi-ai` and `@mariozechner/pi-agent-core` import and run in the Electron main process or a utility process, without embedding `pi-coding-agent` or its tools.\n- [ ] A deterministic local Pi-compatible provider streams a response across the privileged boundary; no network credentials are required for automated evidence.\n- [ ] Packaged-asset, IPC callback, stream, cancellation, and close-lifecycle evidence is recorded.\n- [ ] Electron, Chromium, Node, V8, package, operating-system, and architecture versions and artifact size are recorded.\n- [ ] Windows packaging and real Codex/OpenCode login requirements are documented when unavailable locally.\n- [ ] Disposable spike code is clearly separated from production implementation.\n\n## Product direction\n\nElectron is a fallback comparison. Prefer Tauri if it can satisfy the static shell and optional provider boundaries without disproportionate sidecar complexity.\n\n## Blocked by\n\nNone — can start immediately.","files":null}]}